course: dictionary
lesson: 3590
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The clues around it tell you which one the writer means. In a nursery rhyme, «Old King Cole called for his fiddlers three» is about people who play music, because a king would call for musicians to play at his feast.
explain: A fiddler is a person who plays the fiddle, which is another name for a violin, often in folk, country or Irish music at a dance called a ceilidh. Now read: «Male fiddler crabs wave one giant claw to attract females and warn rivals.» Here a fiddler is a small crab, not a musician, because the words about claws and waving tell you so.
explain: Always ask: what word would fit here? Try your meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense. If you wonder whether a fiddler is a musician or a crab, the words beside it will settle it.
fact: A fiddler is a person who plays the fiddle, which is a violin.
fact: A fiddler crab is a small crab where the male has one huge claw that he waves.
fact: «Fiddler» can also mean someone who cheats a little, such as changing numbers on forms to get money (UK, informal).
fact: Context clues, such as the words about music or claws, tell you which meaning of a word is right.
exercise: «Old King Cole called for his fiddlers three.» What is a fiddler here? | *A person who plays music on a fiddle | A small crab with one big claw | Someone who cheats a little | A dancer at a ceilidh
exercise: «Male fiddler crabs wave one giant claw.» What does the male fiddler crab wave? | *One giant claw | Its little eyes | A flag on a stick | A fiddle with four strings
exercise: In UK informal talk, someone who changes numbers on forms to get money is called a fiddler. What does the word mean in that sense? | A small crab | A folk musician | A kind of dance | *Someone who cheats a little
test: «a folk fiddler» means a musician who plays folk music. What kind of music might a folk fiddler play? | *Folk, country or Irish music | Music made by a computer alone | Heavy metal rock | Only opera at a big city theatre
test: Why do male fiddler crabs wave one giant claw? | *To attract females and warn rivals | To eat their food more quickly | To cheat people out of money on forms | To swim faster through the sea
exam: In «The fiddler played all night at the ceilidh», what is the fiddler doing? | Swimming in a river | Waving one giant claw | *Playing music | Cheating on a form
